From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Clamp the USB4 outputs across system
 sleep

A USB4 router that is kept across s2idle leaves the combo PHY
initialised and powered in USB4 mode while the router's MCU is halted.
The PHY has no system sleep callbacks, so its USB4 outputs stay
unclamped for the whole sleep.

Add system sleep callbacks that clear CLAMP_EN in the USB4 always-on
clamp register at suspend while the USB4 PHY is initialised, which
engages the I/O clamp as autonomous mode does, and set it again at
resume. The router is a consumer of the PHY, so its callbacks run
before these on suspend and after them on resume.

The sequence matches what the platform's Windows driver does around
standby on the Surface Laptop 8.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index e476451840b..2c38ebbad73 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -5211,7 +5211,38 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A USB4 router kept across system suspend leaves the PHY initialized and
+ * powered while its MCU is halted. Clamp the USB4 outputs meanwhile, as
+ * autonomous mode does; the router's callbacks run before ours on suspend
+ * and after ours on resume.
+ */
+static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qmp_combo *qmp = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	guard(mutex)(&qmp->phy_mutex);
+	if (qmp->usb4_init_count && qmp->pcs_aon &&
+	    qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_PCS_USB4_CLAMP_ENABLE])
+		qphy_clrbits(qmp->pcs_aon, qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_PCS_USB4_CLAMP_ENABLE],
+			     CLAMP_EN);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qmp_combo *qmp = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	guard(mutex)(&qmp->phy_mutex);
+	if (qmp->usb4_init_count && qmp->pcs_aon &&
+	    qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_PCS_USB4_CLAMP_ENABLE])
+		qphy_setbits(qmp->pcs_aon, qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_PCS_USB4_CLAMP_ENABLE],
+			     CLAMP_EN);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qmp_combo_pm_ops = {
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qmp_combo_suspend, qmp_combo_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qmp_combo_runtime_suspend,
 			   qmp_combo_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
